            <ArticleTitle>Retroperitoneal cystic lymphangioma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>607-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An interesting and rare differential diagnosis for a retroperitoneal cystic mass is cystic lymphangioma. A case of a patient presenting with a multicystic mass in the retroperitoneum that was identified as a cystic lymphangioma is reported. These tumours are commonly confused with other cystic masses in the retroperitoneum.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
